# Liquid Flow Meter

Swing client + Raspberry Pi UDP server that dispense a user-requested amount of
liquid (alcohol or beverage) through a GPIO-controlled valve. Originally a
SYSC 3010 course project, modernized to Java 21 / Maven and Python 3.

## Repository layout

```
pom.xml                              Maven build (Java 21, JUnit 5)
src/main/java/com/santoyo/...        Swing client
src/test/java/com/santoyo/...        JUnit 5 tests
python/udp_ip_server.py              UDP dispenser server (runs on the Pi)
python/json_update.py                Small helper to edit data.json
.github/workflows/build.yml          CI build
```

## Build & run the Java client

Requires JDK 21 and Maven 3.9+.

```bash
mvn package
java -jar target/liquid-flow-meter-2.0.0.jar
```

The dispenser host defaults to `10.0.0.30`. Override with:

```bash
java -Ddispenser.host=192.168.1.42 -jar target/liquid-flow-meter-2.0.0.jar
```

## Run the dispenser server (Raspberry Pi)

```bash
python3 python/udp_ip_server.py --host 0.0.0.0 \
    --alcohol-port 42000 --beverage-port 43000
```

On non-Pi machines `RPi.GPIO` is stubbed so the server still runs for testing.

## Tests

```bash
mvn test
```

Swing UI smoke tests use AssertJ-Swing and require a display; they are skipped
when `-Djava.awt.headless=true` (the CI default).

## Code style

Formatting is enforced by [Spotless](https://github.com/diffplug/spotless) using
the Palantir Java Format and is checked during `mvn verify`. To auto-fix:

```bash
mvn spotless:apply
```

## Native installer (optional)

Requires JDK 21 with `jpackage` on PATH (and platform tooling: WiX on Windows,
`dpkg`/`rpm` on Linux, Xcode CLT on macOS).

```bash
mvn -Pjpackage package
# output in target/jpackage/
```

